    "goal": "Plate primary human hepatocytes in collagen-sandwich culture in a single well of a 24-well plate at the standard published plating density.",
    "rationale": "Primary human hepatocytes (PHH) are the gold-standard liver cell and do not divide in vitro, so the plating density is the working density. The physiology registry lists the PHH seeding density range as 100,000-200,000 cells/cm2; the standard published collagen-sandwich plating density is ~150,000 cells/cm2 (within that range). A 24-well plate has ~1.9 cm2 growth area, giving ~285,000 cells/well. PHH are human primary material (BSL-2).",
